    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "# Reuse a study\n\nA published GeoLocator Data Package contains everything a study produced: the tags, the raw measurements, the labels and the trajectories of all its birds. This chapter shows how to find a package, read it, join its tables, and bring a tag back into GeoPressureR. We use the [South African Woodland Kingfisher](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13829929) study as an example. To compare many studies, see [Compare studies with the Master](geolocator-master.qmd).\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(GeoLocatoR)\nlibrary(GeoPressureR)\nlibrary(tidyverse)\ntheme_set(theme_minimal(base_size = 12) + theme(panel.grid.minor = element_blank()))\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Find a dataset\n\nBrowse published packages with the [GeoLocatorExplorer](https://geopressure.org/GeoLocatorExplorer/), or directly in the [geolocator-dp Zenodo community](https://zenodo.org/communities/geolocator-dp).\n\n[![<small>GeoLocatorExplorer interface to browse published geolocator data packages.</small>](assets/geolocatorexplorer.png){width=\"100%\" alt=\"Screenshot of GeoLocatorExplorer showing searchable geolocator data packages\"}](https://geopressure.org/GeoLocatorExplorer/)\n\n## Read a package\n\n`read_zenodo()` takes a Zenodo record id, a DOI or a Zenodo URL. It downloads the files, upgrades the package to the latest GeoLocator DP version if needed, and returns a `geolocatordp` object.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\npkg <- read_zenodo(\"13829929\")\n```\n:::\n\n\nA record id or DOI can be a *version* (one fixed release) or a *concept* (all versions, resolving to the latest). `13829929` is the concept id of this study, so `pkg$id` gives the version actually read: keep it with your results. `read_zenodo()` downloads every table of the package, including the raw `measurements`. To read only some tables, see [Read only the tables you need](geolocator-master.qmd#read-only-the-tables-you-need).\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nprint(pkg)\n## \n## ── A GeoLocator Data Package `pkg` (v1.2) ──────────────────────────────────────\n## \n## ── Metadata\n## Note: All green texts are fields of `pkg` which can be accessed with\n## `pkg$field`.\n## • title: \"GeoLocator Data Package: South African Woodland Kingfisher\"\n## • id: <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15259676>\n## • contributors:\n##   Raphaël Nussbaumer (contactperson) - <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8185-1020>\n##   Yann Rime (researcher) - <https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7264-6753>\n##   Samuel Temidayo Osinubi (datacollector) -\n##   <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5143-6985>\n## ✔ access: Open access\n## • licenses: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (cc-by-4.0) -\n##   <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode>\n## • description: \"This repository contains the raw data and the trajectory\n##   information generated with the GeoPressureR workflow, following the\n##   GeoLocator Data Package standard. The more complete code used to generate\n##   this datapackage can be found on the Github Reposit...\"\n## • version: \"v1.2.1\"\n## • codeRepository: <https://github.com/Rafnuss/WoodlandKingfisher>\n## ✔ community: Geolocator DP community\n## • relatedIdentifiers:\n##   issupplementto <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2024.2633>\n## • keywords: \"Woodland Kingfisher\", \"multi-sensor geolocator\", \"intra-african\n##   migration\", \"bird\", and \"migration\"\n## • created: 2025-04-22 06:44:20.918179\n## • bibliographicCitation: \"Nussbaumer R, Rime Y, Osinubi S (2025). \\\"GeoLocator\n##   Data Package: South African Woodland Kingfisher.\\\"\n##   doi:10.5281/zenodo.13829929 <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13829929>.\n##   <https://zenodo.org/records/15259676>.\"\n## • temporal: \"2017-01-10\" to \"2019-09-28\"\n## • taxonomic: \"Halcyon senegalensis\"\n## • numberTags: tags: 25, measurements: 5, light: 5, pressure: 5, activity: 5,\n##   temperature_external: 5, magnetic: 5, paths: 5, pressurepaths: 5\n## \n## ── Resources: (8 resources)\n## • `tags()` (n=25)\n## • `observations()` (n=64)\n## • `measurements()` (n=1,924,975)\n## • `staps()` (n=223)\n## • `twilights()` (n=3,262)\n## • `paths()` (n=22,523)\n## • `edges()` (n=22,018)\n## • `pressurepaths()` (n=224,828)\n```\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nplot(pkg, \"map\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-36011f894cb4445429d9\" style=\"width:100%;height:580px;\" class=\"leaflet html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-36011f894cb4445429d9\">{\"x\":{\"options\":{\"crs\":{\"crsClass\":\"L.CRS.EPSG3857\",\"code\":null,\"proj4def\":null,\"projectedBounds\":null,\"options\":{}}},\"calls\":[{\"method\":\"addTiles\",\"args\":[\"https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png\",null,null,{\"minZoom\":0,\"maxZoom\":18,\"tileSize\":256,\"subdomains\":\"abc\",\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"tms\":false,\"noWrap\":false,\"zoomOffset\":0,\"zoomReverse\":false,\"opacity\":1,\"zIndex\":1,\"detectRetina\":false,\"attribution\":\"&copy; <a href=\\\"https://openstreetmap.org/copyright/\\\">OpenStreetMap<\\/a>,  <a href=\\\"https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/\\\">ODbL<\\/a>\"}]},{\"method\":\"addPolylines\",\"args\":[[[[{\"lng\":[28.76857325,26.625,26.375,27.125,26.625,27.375,25.625,24.125,24.125,24.625,24.625,25.625,25.375,24.625,24.125,23.625,24.375,24.875,25.375,25.375,25.625,26.125,26.375,26.375,26.375,26.125,27.375,23.875,23.375,23.125,26.125,26.125,26.375,25.875,25.125,25.875,25.125,25.125,25.125,26.125,27.375,28.125,28.875,28.76857325],\"lat\":[-22.72463163,-20.125,-18.875,-18.125,-17.125,-17.125,-15.625,-12.375,-11.875,-11.625,-10.375,-8.875,-3.875,-2.125,-0.375,1.125,1.875,1.875,2.625,4.625,5.375,5.875,7.125,7.875,8.125,8.375,8.875,4.375,1.625,-0.625,-3.375,-4.375,-4.125,-7.625,-8.125,-8.625,-9.125,-9.875,-12.125,-13.375,-15.125,-18.125,-21.375,-22.72463163]}]]],null,null,{\"interactive\":true,\"className\":\"\",\"stroke\":true,\"color\":\"#E41A1C\",\"weight\":2,\"opacity\":0.